  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enabling environment for seed companies in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project on the strengthening Egypt&#x2019;s Seed Sector contributes to Egypt&#x2019;s ambition to become a seed hub for Africa. Currently, the country&#x2019;s seed sector faces regulatory challenges that hinder seed companies from introducing climate-smart crop varieties. These limitations affect plant variety protection, variety registration, and alignment with international standards, creating obstacles for both domestic and international seed companies.This project facilitates improvement of the enabling environment for seed companies in Egypt, particularly by strengthening the regulatory framework. This will facilitate the introduction of salt-tolerant, heat-resistant, and water-efficient crop varieties, which are crucial for tackling climate change challenges such as drought, soil degradation, and rising temperatures.To achieve this, the project will develop an Egypt-Netherlands Seed Road Map, establish specialised working groups on key regulatory topics, and initiate a digital seed portal.By addressing regulatory barriers, the project will encourage investment, accelerate the availability of climate-resilient seeds, and enhance Egypt&apos;s trade position. Ultimately, this initiative supports the country&#x2019;s agricultural sector.</narrative>
  </description>
